## Program Outcome

Deliver and release a proportional, revision-bound Idea Brief readiness review that runs only from
the two accepted triggers, blocks unsafe promotion truthfully, transfers legitimate uncertainty as
named PRM gates, preserves ordinary brainstorming responsiveness, and closes the originating Idea
loop against current product and target evidence.

## Milestones And Evidence Gates

### M1-CONTRACT-AUTHORITY-FROZEN — Review contract and structured authority

Status: complete
Evidence: work/evidence/idea-readiness-m1-contract-authority.json; CAMP-0120

Outcome: Freeze the two-trigger boundary, verdict and error semantics, freshness/version contract,
stale-write behavior, structured authority, and minimal generated presentation.

Gates:

- `G1-FAILURE-CONCURRENCY-CONTRACT`: `REVIEW-ERROR` and `REVIEW-UNAVAILABLE` are distinct from
  `NOT-READY`; unavailable review fails promotion closed; an Idea revision changed during review
  makes the result stale and prevents its write or reuse.
- `G2-STRUCTURED-RESULT-AUTHORITY`: one managed structured authority is selected by proving reuse of
  current SQLite primitives or justifying the smallest schema addition; all views are generated and
  direct SQL is outside the operating contract.

Candidate campaign: `freeze-adaptive-readiness-contract-and-authority`.

### M2-PRM-INTEGRATION-PROVEN — Trigger, transfer, and operator flow

Status: complete
Evidence: work/evidence/idea-readiness-m2-integration.json; CAMP-0121

Depends on: M1.

Outcome: Implement both entry points and the focused operator dialogue without adding semantic
review to ordinary brainstorming.

Gates:

- `G3-LOSSLESS-PRM-GATE-TRANSFER`: an exact transfer check proves that every named
  `READY-WITH-PRM-GATES` item appears in accepted PRM state; promotion fails closed if any item is
  omitted.
- `G4-INTERACTION-PORTABILITY`: interrupted dialogue resumes without repeating settled questions;
  semantic judgment is provider-neutral; ordinary brainstorming performs only bounded freshness
  comparison and has no semantic-review latency.

Candidate campaign: `integrate-adaptive-readiness-with-brainstorm-and-prm`.

### M3-RELEASE-QUALIFIED-RECONCILED — Compatibility, release, and closed loop

Status: complete
Evidence: work/evidence/idea-readiness-m3-release-reconciliation.json; CAMP-0122; Tool Shed v0.37.0

Depends on: M2.

Outcome: Qualify, publish, canary, and reconcile the feature through the maintainer-first upgrade
path and a disconnected production-shaped client.

Gate:

- `G5-UPGRADE-ADAPTIVE-QUALIFICATION`: versioned contracts and older-client rejection of unknown
  verdicts/versions pass; simple, moderate, and consequential fixtures prove adaptive scope; both
  triggers, stale reuse, concurrent change, failure paths, zero ordinary-brainstorm review, and
  lossless gate transfer pass; release provenance, maintainer synchronization, client canary, and
  origin-to-product reconciliation account for all accepted requirements and material development
  changes.

Candidate campaign: `qualify-release-and-reconcile-adaptive-readiness-review`.

